  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "New: SemanticSearchField, a write-only field without UI that makes the rows of a module searchable by meaning from the AI chat. On Submit it turns the source fields of the row into a text (one line per field, display name: value; candidates and links by display text, dates in ISO form, LF line breaks) and sends it; the server (Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras.Server 0.14.0) adds the embedding vector and both are stored in write-only columns (DbColumnText, DbColumnVector as a JSON array text). The similarity is computed by the database: DbColumnVectorSearch names the vector-typed column (a pgvector generated column cast from DbColumnVector on PostgreSQL, or the VECTOR column itself on SQL Server 2025). All three columns are required (design check SemanticSearchFieldDesign:1) and modules on other databases are indexed but not searchable. The field implements IDataDependentField so its SourceFields are loaded with it; design check SemanticSearchFieldDesign:2 reports a detail layout that loads only part of the source fields. The field exposes Reindex() / ReindexMissing() / CancelReindex() to scripts (rebuild the text and vector of all readable rows, or only of the rows without a vector, as a server job; progress in IsReindexing / ReindexProcessed / ReindexTotal, the result in ReindexError and the OnReindexCompleted script), so a ButtonField anywhere in the module can start it; the host sets SemanticSearchField.EndPoint to its controller (see Codeer.LowCode.Blazor.Extras.Server). Requires Codeer.LowCode.Blazor 1.3.35.",
